WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.959
in the last episode we went over the main secrets in the DLC and

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:10.529
As I'm sure you noticed it's so easy to think you found everything, but there's always more secrets tucked away

00:00:12.549 --> 00:00:17.278
For example until very recently I did not know Midir had a grab attack

00:00:18.699 --> 00:00:26.009
When I first beat Midir it was with a silver knight leader cosplay and in the five hours it took to deplete Midir's

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:30.209
Gigantic health pool, I remember continuously thinking "Man

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:34.709
Ledo could have looked so much better" because a few days before release

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.939
hundreds of assets were data mined from the Ring City patch and

00:00:39.309 --> 00:00:44.669
Amongst these were the Ui icons for a certain armour set look closely at it

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.840
So it's a well worn silver knight set and it has a few extra

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:55.079
Modifications to set it apart from the other standard sets of the legion just look at those horns

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:59.879
It would have been so perfect for ledo because he's described as an eccentric

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:06.659
Silver Knight a man wearing well-worn armor from his distant travels around the outskirts of the world

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:12.239
Another thing that didn't make it in are a few more lines of dialogue from the locust preacher

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:18.629
This creature gives exposition on many characters of Dark Souls 3 and if my source is correct

00:01:18.729 --> 00:01:25.169
he was supposed to also say "Of all the fingers he alone was embraced by the Abyss, for

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:31.229
he was human and never a grub, fear not the dark my friend and let the feast again

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:35.819
So he's describing a finger of Rosaria, but which one

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:42.959
For a little bit of background fingers of Rosaria our red phantoms who invade kill and pillage

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:49.829
For their own benefit and to gather tongues for their mistress in return they can be reborn

00:01:50.259 --> 00:01:55.769
Though those who are reborn one too many times run the risk of turning into grubs

00:01:56.350 --> 00:02:03.059
something that does happen to Yellow Finger Hazel in fact "Of all the fingers, he alone was embraced by the Abyss,

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:11.240
For he was human and never a grub" so place your bets who do you think this is describing? There are only really three

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:18.169
options for there are only three male fingers of Rosaria: Creighton the Wanderer, Ring finger Leonard and

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:20.550
Middle Finger Kirk

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:23.749
Personally I think it's Leonard in this dialogue

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:29.660
He was the one who eventually stole Rosaria's soul in some misguided effort to keep it safe

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:36.350
I believe he's the finger in question because the dialogue says he was human and never a grub and

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:43.490
Leonard is described multiple times as rejecting rebirth and the restoration of his scarred Flesh

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:50.869
therefore unlike the other fingers he would never risk turning into a grub and losing his humanity

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:59.000
of course for whatever reason this dialogue was removed which makes it unwise to draw conclusions, but it is interesting nonetheless

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:06.439
For what does it mean to be embraced by the abyss that's something we'll go into in our locust video

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:08.440
I promised so keep an eye for that

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:16.790
Speaking of locusts. Have you ever tried to listen to the locusts below the swamp they say a variation...

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:19.750
and

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:30.010
While I was straining my ears listening for this fairly pointless dialogue, so I could fill out my 20 questions

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:33.519
I noticed that the abdomen of the locusts is

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:39.999
Remarkably similar to that of the angels look at the Iridescent wings and the stinger in particular

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:45.820
Are these reused assets or is there some parallel to be drawn between the two creatures?

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:51.249
Or am I trying really hard to make this a valid point to include in the video who knows?

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:58.570
Just above the locusts is Lapp in what can potentially be the last place you meet him -

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:03.640
"Please someone tell me who am I?"

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:06.520
Why am I here?

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:11.140
Keep revisiting him here and after reloading the game three times

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:15.820
We get solid proof that Lapp was not lying about forgetting his name

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:20.799
And he was not lying about going hollow if you make him hostile here

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:24.340
You can unlock a more satisfying ending to Lapp's story

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:30.310
The Lapp Arc of Patches Quest line is really well executed

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:36.520
and you have to love the clues they give you from the signature squat the slightly tuned voice and

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:42.429
Especially the part where he risks his life to find you treasure if you failed to pick it up

00:04:42.919 --> 00:04:46.599
But did you know that it was always possible to guess who Lapp was?

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:49.360
simply from his name

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.759
a Lappe is a word in Middle high German

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:55.390
that is used to describe a simple-Minded person or

00:04:55.550 --> 00:05:02.290
It's ironically used to call a smart person a fool and obviously this suit Lapp to an insane

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:04.600
Degree because he's both lost his mind

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:11.409
And it's ironic that of all the intelligent people to lose their minds it would be our best friend Patches

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:14.890
furthermore in Middle High German the name Lapp

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:22.929
Also refers to a mender of clothes or shoes and was used to describe a cloth a rag or a patch

00:05:23.419 --> 00:05:26.139
Lapp also means patch in Swedish

00:05:27.919 --> 00:05:34.299
Anyway after you've talked to Lapp about the ring City. You can track this information back to its source

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:41.399
Why where did you hear name love? Oh, it doesn't matter. I'll tell you what I know

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:47.459
The Rings City is said to be at world's end

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:52.590
Past this heap of rubbish as far as one can go

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:55.470
But you better think twice

00:05:55.870 --> 00:06:02.040
the Forsaken Ring City was walled off by the gods to contain the pygmies and

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:07.020
The Dark Soul is better left well alone

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:11.309
Number eight have you noticed what I'm zooming towards

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:14.879
These parts of the dreg heap are on an endless trip

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:21.480
Downwards and you have to wonder are they meant to provide the illusion from a distance that the dreg heap is

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:26.789
collapsing downwards and inwards or was this just an asset that they forgot to lock in place and

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:31.379
Some dreg heap assets should feature more prominently in my opinion

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:39.360
For example if you look left at the very edge of the drop down to the Demon prince you can see the entire undead settlement

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:41.710
cobbled together here and

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:44.399
further down in the Demon Prince Arena

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:52.560
there's the rubble of the first firelink shrine you can even find the well and the stones Dead circle at the center and

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:56.609
Of course don't forget this part of the Grand archives

00:06:57.430 --> 00:07:00.359
This rooftop you can jump to in early Lothric

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:07.260
This room where you first encounter Lothric knights, the courtyard in Lothric with two enormous snakes

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:09.430
wait what

00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:16.440
I had this tweeted at me by @BestSiegmeyer on Twitter who discovered these giant ash coated snakes

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:21.570
That bleed he posits that they might be primordial serpents

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:29.429
But if they are they certainly lack the familiar features the signature nose the teeth the moustache thing

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:33.330
No, whatever these are I'm not sure they're from any age

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:40.289
We know of, note however that they are impaled with the weapons of the Lothric knights as if a battle took place here

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:44.369
Number 11 with every major drop in the dreg heap

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:50.580
there's the ghost of Gael to guide you but, did you notice also he's ripped off a part of his red cloak and

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:56.760
Weighed it down with a stone these additional markers show you where to go I bet

00:07:56.760 --> 00:08:01.650
He regrets it now that cloak probably could have done with the extra range in the boss fight

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:07.589
The most significant piece of red cloth is located in the shared grave of the ring City

00:08:08.140 --> 00:08:11.879
Signifying the drops downwards that's necessary to progress you upwards

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:16.199
Speaking of does Patches really screw you over with his final kick

