00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:21.540
Interestingly enough though there are these statues that you found around

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:28.019
Irithyll though who they're of has always been a bit of a mystery and given that they're meant to be out of eyeshot

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:33.599
I doubt this is much more than a reused asset and never meant to be seen up close

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:37.169
and my God were some things not meant to be seen up close

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:43.879
In the world brought to ruin by the breaking of the shell are two crumbled kingdoms off in the distance

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:48.499
One is Lothric 100% is even a 3D model

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:50.720
You can get close to and look at properly

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:58.160
But further in a blurry 2d asset at the edge of the end of the world is this structure?

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:04.160
It has elements of Anor Londo it has elements of that old Drangleic footage

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:04.770
we saw

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:06.140
but whichever it is

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:13.789
I think that they're trying to convey that this place at the end of the world contains the ruins of the most significant kingdoms and

00:10:14.310 --> 00:10:19.120
Lothric being featured so prominently here leads me to believe that our

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:21.300
Unkindled Adventure© was

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:28.980
potentially the most significant of all, as an aside this place at the end is what you saw in the opening cutscene

