00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:52.229
Another theory I've seen about the egg has been thrown around ever since

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:56.969
Filianore's design was shown and it talks about the resemblance between

00:12:57.160 --> 00:13:02.760
Filianore's egg and the vagrants of Dark Souls 1 and have to agree. Then is a resemblance

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:08.399
Look at them. They're cracked in much the same way with a coarse dark interior and

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:15.089
Remember these creatures were only present in Dark Souls 1 which was during the close of the age of the gods

00:13:15.279 --> 00:13:22.739
So even from a timeline point of view it makes sense that Filianore who was likely placed here in the age of the gods

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:25.950
May have possessed one of the last vagrants

00:13:26.230 --> 00:13:27.640
these mysterious creatures

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:34.679
Used to appear in other people's worlds if you dropped items or if you lost a large amount of humanity in your own world

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:41.010
and very very interestingly the cracked vagrants simply drop humanity and Twin humanity

00:13:41.680 --> 00:13:47.940
Suggesting that the humanity fragments of the dark soul might have made up that dark interior

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:54.990
And for an egg with a black inside that obscures the dark soul of humanity from those who would claim it

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:57.420
this feels very significant

